# tela/proof/extension-forms/src/forms.fab — formslib — the forms component
# family (the Stage 4 independent-extension proof, provider `formslib`).
#
# Stage 4 U2 (component-family — the static half). A SEPARATE package from
# the kernel (own faber.toml, own provider identity `formslib`, imported
# through the benchmark library-home machinery). The identity freeze +
# authoring constraints come from the U1 discovery record
# (stage-4-discovery.md).
#
# The family (four surface groups per the delivery U2 done_when (b)):
#   field (text input)    — field / FieldProps   → form-field-<name>
#   checkbox              — checkbox / CheckboxProps     → form-checkbox-<name>
#   select                — select / SelectProps → form-select-<name>
#   error/live-region association — error_region (→ form-error-<name>,
#     the identity a field's aria-describedby references) + form_live_region
#     (the form-level live region, form-live) + field_group (the field
#     group: field + error node under form-control-<name>).
# The keyboard/validation structure is DECLARED here: the field/checkbox/
# select are natively focusable (native field semantics — Tab reaches them
# directly, the campaign §8 keyboard contract); the form-level
# focus-move/validation behavior belongs to the app-typed plan (U4).
#
# G4 consumability record (per export, the stage-1 §3 + U1 §4.2 evidence;
# reconciled by U0 after cds-u6 + the live exempla-mode probe):
#   - The `→ tela.View` component fns (field/select/checkbox/error_region/
#     form_live_region/field_group) reference the imported sibling type
#     tela.View in their signatures. cds-u6 (file-interface-exports) landed:
#     the U0 probe re-verified exempla-mode consumption of `→ tela.View`
#     fns against live radix — GREEN (radix check + TS emit + assembly +
#     node execute). The package KEEPS its seam (never a duplicated View
#     in the package); the exempla consume the component fns through
#     normal qualified imports; the `_html` string-returning render helpers
#     are RETIRED (the exempla-mode workaround surface is obsolete).
#   - Cross-package consumption (probed, U2 close): `forms.field(
#     forms.field_props(...))` (direct call result as an argument) and
#     `forms.field_props(...).name` (field access on the call result)
#     resolve from a consumer; binding the constructor result to a `const`
#     with inferred type hits the provider-interface inference gap
#     (PARSE001 — the recorded G4/dialect family). The consumer composes
#     with the direct-call pattern.
#
# fix:<id> markers:
#   fix:g4 — REMOVED (cds-u6 landed + the U0 exempla-mode probe re-verified
#     `→ tela.View` consumption green; the `*_html` helpers + the
#     compose-without posture are RETIRED).
#   fix:g5 — NONE: field/checkbox/select/error_region/form_live_region/
#     field_group/field_props/checkbox_props/select_props probed
#     collision-free on in-tree radix 0.80.0 (a free fn may share a class
#     name — G5's collision is enum-member-specific).
#   fix:snapshot-name-collision — the props classes (FieldProps/
#     SelectProps/CheckboxProps) avoid kernel type names (Space/Style/
#     Token/Theme/EventName/Effect/Update/View/…) AND the canary-app's
#     plan type names (ControlProps/EventBinding/Message — the app-typed plan
#     in U3/U4 lives app-side; the forms package keeps distinct names).
#     MF-7 resolution (U0): the per-package token carriers (`Scopulus`/
#     `Scopula_formae`) are DELETED — the kernel `Token` is the ONE
#     token-carrier pattern; the snapshot-collision removal predicate was
#     re-verified live (two providers declaring the same-named class +
#     a consumer checks clean on in-tree radix 0.80.0).
#   fix:codegen001 — Rust emit-across-imports persists (the TS lane is the
#     proven lane; recorded, never the gate).
#   fix:sem001 — HELD (U4): consumers read effect keys through
#     tela.effect_identity, never matching an imported union (the
#     G3-family imported-union match does not bind from a consumer); the
#     app-typed plan owns its message union, which is app-local.
#
# Stage 4 U4 (behavior-semantics) — the behavior contract + the pure
# validation-mapping surface. The components' documented
# event/identity/validation contract (below) is the semantics the
# consumer's plan relies on (the app-typed proof lives app-side in
# canary-app/src/main.fab — the D1 app-typed boundary, recorded). The
# SHARED-SOURCE statement: the same components that render statically in
# U2 carry the behavior contract; the interactive execution is U7 (gated —
# the dom-shim is not the interactive claim).
#
# The behavior contract (per component — the event surface, the identity
# scheme, the ARIA/validation semantics):
#   field (text input)  — identity form-field-<name>; events: "input"
#     (each text entry — the live-validation event) + "click" (pointer
#     activation on the native input); validation: aria-invalid
#     "true"/"false" + aria-describedby → form-error-<name> when invalid;
#     the error text lives in the associated error node (the field_group
#     association, U2).
#   checkbox            — identity form-checkbox-<name>; events: "change"
#     (toggle) + "click"; aria-checked "true"/"false" + the invalid
#     surface (aria-invalid + aria-describedby → form-error-<name>).
#   select              — identity form-select-<name>; events: "change"
#     (selection change) + "click"; the invalid surface (aria-invalid +
#     aria-describedby → form-error-<name>).
#   form-level submit   — event "submit": the family declares the stable
#     spelling (submit_event); the U2 static surface renders no
#     <form> element, so the submit source is the app-declared form
#     aggregate — the app-typed plan owns it (D1: the concrete plan is the
#     application's surface, never kernel-generic).
#   live region         — identity form-live; role=status +
#     aria-live=polite; the announcement policy: announce on a
#     validation-state change, silent on no-op (the Stage 3 §1.5 pattern
#     extended to form validation) — carried by the app-typed plan.
# The event-name constants + the validation-state mapping fns (the U4
# surface at the end of this module) are pure string/bool signatures —
# G4-safe (they stay on the exported file interface; the consumer's plan
# builds on them without the WARN014 family). fix:g5 — the new identifiers
# (field_event/change_event/submit_event/click_event/
# invalid_state/error_present) probed collision-free on in-tree radix
# 0.80.0.

import from "tela:tela" public * ut tela

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Typed props (per-component state carriers — local classes, consumable).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The field (text input) props. `invalid` = "true"/"false" (aria-invalid);
# `error` = the error message ("" = none — the group renders an empty error
# node; aria-describedby → form-error-<name> when invalid).
class FieldProps {
    string name
    string label
    string value
    string invalid
    string error
}

# The select props (option list; aria-invalid + aria-describedby surface).
class SelectProps {
    string name
    string label
    list<string> options
    string invalid
}

# The checkbox props. `selected` = "true"/"false" (aria-checked).
class CheckboxProps {
    string name
    string label
    string selected
    string invalid
}

# Props constructors — ordinary functions returning local classes, keeping
# the provider boundary consumable.
fn field_props(string name, string label, string value, string invalid, string error) → FieldProps {
    return FieldProps { name = name, label = label, value = value, invalid = invalid, error = error }
}

fn select_props(string name, string label, list<string> options, string invalid) → SelectProps {
    return SelectProps { name = name, label = label, options = options, invalid = invalid }
}

fn checkbox_props(string name, string label, string selected, string invalid) → CheckboxProps {
    return CheckboxProps { name = name, label = label, selected = selected, invalid = invalid }
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The field (text input) — form-field-<name>.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn field(FieldProps props) → tela.View {
    var list<tela.Attribute> attributes ← vacua
    attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "type", value = "text" })
    attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "aria-label", value = props.label })
    attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "aria-invalid", value = props.invalid })
    if props.invalid ≡ "true" {
        attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "aria-describedby", value = "form-error-" + props.name })
    }
    if not (props.value ≡ "") {
        attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "value", value = props.value })
    }
    return tela.element_full(
        tela.new_identity("form-field-" + props.name),
        tela.html_space(),
        "input",
        attributes,
        [],
        []
    )
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The checkbox — form-checkbox-<name> (aria-checked + the invalid surface).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn checkbox(CheckboxProps props) → tela.View {
    var list<tela.Attribute> attributes ← vacua
    attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "type", value = "checkbox" })
    attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "aria-label", value = props.label })
    attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "aria-checked", value = props.selected })
    attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "aria-invalid", value = props.invalid })
    if props.invalid ≡ "true" {
        attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "aria-describedby", value = "form-error-" + props.name })
    }
    return tela.element_full(
        tela.new_identity("form-checkbox-" + props.name),
        tela.html_space(),
        "input",
        attributes,
        [],
        []
    )
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The select — form-select-<name> (native option children).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn select(SelectProps props) → tela.View {
    var list<tela.Attribute> attributes ← vacua
    attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "aria-label", value = props.label })
    attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "aria-invalid", value = props.invalid })
    if props.invalid ≡ "true" {
        attributes.appende(tela.Attribute { name = "aria-describedby", value = "form-error-" + props.name })
    }
    var list<tela.View> children ← vacua
    var int i ← 0
    while i < props.options.longitudo() {
        children.appende(tela.element_view(tela.html_space(), "option", [ tela.text_view(props.options[i]) ]))
        i ← i + 1
    }
    return tela.element_full(
        tela.new_identity("form-select-" + props.name),
        tela.html_space(),
        "select",
        attributes,
        [],
        children
    )
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The error / live-region association.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The error node for a field: role=alert + the identity the field's
# aria-describedby references (form-error-<name>). Empty text = empty node
# (the association structure is stable — the group always carries it).
fn error_region(string name, string text) → tela.View {
    var list<tela.View> children ← vacua
    if not (text ≡ "") {
        children.appende(tela.text_view(text))
    }
    return tela.element_full(
        tela.new_identity("form-error-" + name),
        tela.html_space(),
        "div",
        [ tela.Attribute { name = "role", value = "alert" } ],
        [],
        children
    )
}

# The form-level live region (the Stage 3 §1.5 pattern extended to forms):
# role=status + aria-live=polite, form-live. The announcement policy (on a
# validation-state change, silent on no-op) is the app-typed plan's (U4).
fn form_live_region() → tela.View {
    return tela.element_full(
        tela.new_identity("form-live"),
        tela.html_space(),
        "div",
        [
            tela.Attribute { name = "role", value = "status" },
            tela.Attribute { name = "aria-live", value = "polite" }
        ],
        [],
        []
    )
}

# The field group — the association surface: the field (aria-describedby →
# form-error-<name> when invalid) + its error node under form-control-<name>.
fn field_group(FieldProps props) → tela.View {
    var list<tela.View> children ← vacua
    children.appende(field(props))
    children.appende(error_region(props.name, props.error))
    return tela.element_full(
        tela.new_identity("form-control-" + props.name),
        tela.html_space(),
        "div",
        [],
        [],
        children
    )
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 4 U3 — namespaced `form.*` theme tokens, the component style
# bundles, and the product-assembly input (the three-package cascade's
# formslib contribution).
#
# Token surface (delivery U3 done_when (a); MF-7 resolution): zero-arg
# accessors returning the KERNEL `tela.Token` carrier (the standardized
# token-carrier pattern — the per-package carriers `Scopulus`/
# `Scopula_formae` are DELETED; the kernel `Token` is the ONE carrier).
# Consumers read fields on the call result (`forms.form_field_invalid()
# .name`/`.value`); token rendering is the kernel's (`theme_css` →
# `--form-field-invalid`). `form.focus` is the focus-ring token.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn form_field_invalid() → tela.Token {
    return tela.Token { name = "form.field.invalid", value = "#dc2626" }
}

fn form_field_valid() → tela.Token {
    return tela.Token { name = "form.field.valid", value = "#16a34a" }
}

fn form_focus() → tela.Token {
    return tela.Token { name = "form.focus", value = "#2563eb" }
}

# The token collection (the package's assembly-input convenience — the
# consumer composes the theme via the individual accessors, the field-access
# pattern; the collection is the package's self-usable summary).
fn form_tokens() → list<tela.Token> {
    return [ form_field_invalid(), form_field_valid(), form_focus() ]
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The family's component style bundle (delivery U3 done_when (b)): rules
# keyed on the family's data-tela identities (the dynamic identities ride
# attribute-prefix selectors), referencing the `--form-*` tokens. The
# Style-returning signature is class-returning → consumable from the
# consumer today (the stage-1 §3 evidence: `→ tela.Style` resolves).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn form_style() → tela.Style {
    return tela.Style {
        rules = [
            tela.Rule {
                selector = "[data-tela^='form-field-']",
                declarations = [
                    tela.Declaration { name = "border-bottom", value = "2px solid var(--form-field-invalid)" },
                    tela.Declaration { name = "color", value = "var(--form-field-valid)" }
                ]
            },
            tela.Rule {
                selector = "[data-tela^='form-field-']:focus",
                declarations = [
                    tela.Declaration { name = "outline", value = "2px solid var(--form-focus)" }
                ]
            },
            tela.Rule {
                selector = "[data-tela^='form-error-']",
                declarations = [
                    tela.Declaration { name = "color", value = "var(--form-field-invalid)" },
                    tela.Declaration { name = "font-size", value = "0.875rem" }
                ]
            },
            tela.Rule {
                selector = "[data-tela='form-live']",
                declarations = [
                    tela.Declaration { name = "font-weight", value = "600" },
                    tela.Declaration { name = "color", value = "var(--form-field-valid)" }
                ]
            },
            tela.Rule {
                selector = "[data-tela^='form-checkbox-']",
                declarations = [
                    tela.Declaration { name = "accent-color", value = "var(--form-field-valid)" }
                ]
            }
        ]
    }
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 4 U4 — the behavior-semantics contract surface.
#
# Event-name accessors keep the consumer plan on the G4-safe string
# surface instead of duplicating event literals.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn field_event() → string {
    return "input"
}

fn change_event() → string {
    return "change"
}

fn submit_event() → string {
    return "submit"
}

fn click_event() → string {
    return "click"
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The validation-state mapping fns (pure string/bool signatures — G4-safe):
#   invalid_state — the validation state → the aria-invalid string
#     ("true"/"false");
#   error_present — the error text → whether the field is invalid (a
#     non-empty error = invalid — the describedby association + the error
#     node are live).
# The app-typed plan's update/validation semantics build on these
# (invalid → aria-invalid + error text; valid → cleared; the no-op rule).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn invalid_state(bool invalid) → string {
    if invalid then return "true"
    return "false"
}

fn error_present(string error) → bool {
    return not (error ≡ "")
}
